**Short Story:**  
Kip the Gnome Warlock trudged through Stranglethorn Vale with his Succubus, Vex, at his side. Vex’s stealth helped him sneak past patrols, and her Lash of Pain finished off tough mobs when he was low. Once, a band of pirates cornered him—he used Soothing Kiss to drop their threat, then ran. Vex’s Seduction even froze a rogue who’d been chasing him. He felt safe, fast, and in control.

**Answer:**  
Voidwalkers are more commonly seen because their threat generation (Torment, Suffering) and survival tools (Consume Shadows, Sacrifice) make them ideal for group content and PvP, where Warlocks often draw attention. Succubus, while better for solo leveling and questing, lacks strong threat tools, so Warlocks in groups switch to Voidwalkers to manage aggro, making Voidwalkers more "visible" in general. [end of text]


